<p>So what does all of this tell us? T1 changes their play-style closer to the world’s season. During the domestic competition period, T1 places a focus on getting kills and picking advantageous team-fights.</p>
<p>As we saw in our first graph, this does get them some wins. But looking at this data we can assume that during the final’s season, T1 recognizes that the key to winning is focusing on objectives opposed to getting kills. While it may result in less flashy game play, it’s clear that it’s the best strategy for securing a win at Worlds finals.</p>



